That's not completely true. I've noticed that I always seem to handle
them without even remembering to wield something of silver, so I did
some "research" on hitting/throwing:

- you can throw/crash potions at shades

- you can beat them to death with a clove of garlic, since they are
  allergic (dmg 1), but you'll have to catch them first

- additionally, nethack mirrors all have a silver layer and thus can
  touch shades for negligible (and expensive!) damage (they don't
  inflict "silver damage" though, just dmg 1)

Fighting:

- if you would do damage anyway, you get your strength bonuses

- blessed gloves still have their bonus when fighting "bare-handed"
  (d4)

- blessed weapons do have it as well (d4)

- artifact bonuses apply

- [a bug?] if you're a samurai firing ya with a yumi or an elf firing
  elven arrows with an elven bow you get your bonus (1)

- [a bug?] you can joust

... in other words, by the time you meet them, they will be worth at
most a couple of hits anyway.

